## 6. Indexing Strategy

```prisma
// ✅ Index every column used in WHERE, ORDER BY, or JOIN
model Post {
  id          String     @id @default(cuid())
  title       String
  slug        String     @unique                  // Unique = auto-indexed
  status      PostStatus
  authorId    String
  publishedAt DateTime?
  createdAt   DateTime   @default(now())

  @@index([authorId])                              // FK lookup
  @@index([status, publishedAt(sort: Desc)])       // "Published posts, newest first"
  @@index([authorId, status, createdAt(sort: Desc)]) // "User's drafts/published, newest"
}
```

**Indexing Rules:**
- Index ALL foreign key columns. PostgreSQL does not auto-index FKs.
- Composite indexes: put equality filters first, range/sort columns last.
  - `@@index([status, createdAt])` → Good for `WHERE status = 'PUBLISHED' ORDER BY createdAt DESC`
  - `@@index([createdAt, status])` → Less efficient for the same query
- Don't over-index: every index slows down writes. Only index columns you actually query.
- Monitor slow queries: `EXPLAIN ANALYZE` on queries taking > 100ms.
- Unique constraints (`@unique`) automatically create indexes.

