## 11. Seeding

```typescript
// prisma/seed.ts
import { PrismaClient } from '@prisma/client';
import bcrypt from 'bcryptjs';

const prisma = new PrismaClient();

async function main() {
  // Create admin user
  const admin = await prisma.user.upsert({
    where: { email: 'admin@example.com' },
    update: {},
    create: {
      email: 'admin@example.com',
      name: 'Admin',
      role: 'ADMIN',
      password: await bcrypt.hash('SecureAdminPass123!', 12),
    },
  });

  // Create sample posts
  await prisma.post.createMany({
    data: [
      { title: 'First Post', slug: 'first-post', content: 'Hello world', status: 'PUBLISHED', authorId: admin.id },
      { title: 'Draft Post', slug: 'draft-post', content: 'Work in progress', status: 'DRAFT', authorId: admin.id },
    ],
    skipDuplicates: true,
  });

  console.log('✅ Seed complete');
}

main()
  .catch(console.error)
  .finally(() => prisma.$disconnect());
```

## Database Checklist

- [ ] Every table has `id`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`
- [ ] All foreign keys have indexes
- [ ] Money/currency uses `Decimal`, never `Float`
- [ ] Public-facing IDs use `cuid()`/`uuid()`, not auto-increment
- [ ] Sensitive columns (password, token) never included in default selects
- [ ] All list queries paginated (never unbounded)
- [ ] Destructive schema changes use multi-step migrations
- [ ] Connection pooling configured for production
- [ ] RLS policies active on all user-data tables (Supabase)
- [ ] Seed script works from clean database
